.TH CMUXR 1 "2026-10-21" "de-xr" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cmuxr \- console and native graphical music player for DomeD
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
cmuxr [--console|--gui|--tray] [--no-gui] [--floor on|off]
      [CMUS-OPTIONS] [--open FILE...]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
cmuxr retains the cmus ncurses/audio engine and defaults to a patched FLTK 1.4.5
graphical frontend. Qt6/PySide6 is retained as an explicit runtime opt-in:
.nf
DE_XR_TOOLKIT=Qt6 cmuxr --gui
.fi
.PP
An interactive terminal defaults to console playback; a graphical nonterminal
launch opens FLTK. Without a display server, the console is used.
Qt6 is not needed for FLTK or console playback. Some launcher help descriptions
still say Qt6 for --gui; the toolkit selection above determines the actual frontend.
Decoded-audio spectrum data drives the optional XR floor without microphone capture.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-console
Start the console, with a graphical companion when available.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-gui
Use the console without a graphical companion.
.TP
.B \-\-gui
Open the selected graphical frontend. Start the console engine on a
pseudoterminal if needed. Repeated GUI launches wake the existing frontend.
.TP
.B \-\-tray
Start hidden when a tray watcher is available; otherwise show a normal window.
.TP
.BI "\-\-floor " on|off
Save the floor preference. Given alone, save and exit; this does not start a
renderer. Use cmuxr-floor for that purpose.
.TP
.BI "\-\-open " FILE...
Play local files or file URIs. Play the first and queue additional selections,
reusing an engine when possible. Formats depend on installed decoder plugins.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print launcher help and exit.
.PP
Other options are forwarded to the cmus engine; see cmus(1).
.SH FLTK CONTROLS
The native form has paged/searchable Playlist, Library and Queue sources,
asynchronous core requests, spectrum, seek and volume controls, command menus
and a StatusNotifierItem tray. Close hides the window if a tray watcher exists;
tray activation reopens it. Without a watcher, tray startup shows a window.
File choosers are native FLTK.
.PP
Enter plays the selection; Space plays or pauses. Ctrl+Left/Right select the
previous/next track; Alt+Left/Right seek. Ctrl+O adds files; Ctrl+E queues the
selection. Delete removes a library entry, leaving the audio file on disk.
F5 refreshes, plus/minus changes volume and Ctrl+Q quits.
.PP
DomeD supplies XR pointer/keyboard input to the ordinary Wayland surface.
Application menus are exported through DBusMenu/KDE AppMenu where supported.
Live DomeD palette and bitmap-font updates require the patched FLTK runtime.
.SH OPTIONAL QT FRONTEND
DE_XR_TOOLKIT=Qt6 selects the retained PySide6 interface. It has folder/history
navigation, File/Playback/Go/Library/View menus and its own shortcuts, including
Ctrl+Shift+O for a folder, Ctrl+L for the path and Ctrl+1/2 for library/playlist.
Its visible_entries compact-view preference is not a FLTK parity claim.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cmuxr/
Engine configuration/library; default ~/.config/cmuxr. CMUS_HOME overrides
this engine directory.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cmuxr/settings.json
Frontend preferences, including floor_enabled and floor_size_m.
The Qt frontend additionally uses visible_entries (4 to 20).
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/dome/appearance.json
DomeD palette/font settings.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/cmuxr-socket
Engine control socket, overridden by CMUS_SOCKET.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/cmuxr-floor.json
Expiring decoded-audio spectrum frames, published up to 20 Hz even in console mode.
.PP
Without XDG_RUNTIME_DIR, console runtime files use a private per-user /tmp
directory. XR spectrum transport requires XDG_RUNTIME_DIR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DE_XR_TOOLKIT
FLTK by default; Qt6 explicitly opts into PySide6. This is a launcher setting,
not a CMake selector for cmuxr's standalone FLTK subdirectory.
.TP
.B CMUXR_FLTK_BINARY
Override the native executable. Otherwise the source build-fltk/cmuxr-fltk
is used if present, then cmuxr-fltk on PATH.
.TP
.B DE_XR_FLTK_PREFIX
Select the matching patched FLTK runtime prefix; its lib directory is prepended
to LD_LIBRARY_PATH. Set this when automatic deployment-prefix discovery fails.
.TP
.B CMUS_HOME, CMUS_SOCKET
Override engine configuration and its Unix socket.
.TP
.B DISPLAY, WAYLAND_DISPLAY
Determine graphical session availability.
.TP
.B PULSE_SINK
Select PulseAudio/PipeWire-Pulse output when the engine uses the ALSA pulse device.
.SH INSTALLATION
The shell installer builds/stages the core, launcher, Python modules and manual.
The default GUI needs an additional native build/stage:
.nf
cmake -S fltk -B build-fltk -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
  -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH=/path/to/patched-fltk-1.4.5
cmake --build build-fltk --parallel
DESTDIR="$PWD/stage" cmake --install build-fltk --prefix /usr/local
.fi
.PP
Build as a regular user and review staged files before privileged installation.
The FLTK GUI requires its patched 1.4.5 shared runtime. Full real-library,
installation/relocation, accessibility/IME and bitmap shaping coverage remains
incomplete; simulated HMD testing does not validate physical WiVRn streaming.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
cmuxr --no-gui
cmuxr --gui
cmuxr --gui --open "$HOME/Music/song.flac"
DE_XR_TOOLKIT=Qt6 cmuxr --gui
cmuxr --floor off
cmuxr-floor --size 3x3
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cmuxr-floor (1),
.BR cmus (1),
.BR cmus-remote (1),
.BR cmus-tutorial (7)
